<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33095" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Osca</span></b> , ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Hispania
			Tarraconensis</i>, now <i>Huesca</i>, in Aragon,
				<i><span class="en">Vell.
				2, 30, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 22, 9</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oscensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Osca</i>, <i>a town of Spain</i>,
				<i>Oscan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 57</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argentum,</span>”
				<i>with the Oscan stamp</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					34, 10</span></i>
			. —In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oscenses</span></b> , ĭum,
				m., <i>the inhabitants of Osca</i>, <i>the Oscans</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				1, 60</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 3, 4, §
		24</span></i>.</div>
